1://! Experimental asynchronous DSA bytes codec for tonic.
2://!
3://! This crate exercises tonic's `Encoder::poll_encode` path with an explicit
4://! in-flight Intel DSA copy. The encoder keeps ordinary CPU encoding as the
5://! default when no work queue is configured. When DSA is enabled, it submits a
6://! memmove descriptor, returns `Poll::Pending`, and finishes the gRPC frame after
7://! the descriptor completion record reaches a terminal status.
8://!
9://! The implementation reserves final `EncodeBuf` storage, assumes that storage
10://! remains stable while `poll_encode` returns `Poll::Pending`, and commits the
11://! initialized bytes after the DSA completion record reaches a terminal status.
